From 881a33018c09fbae41db9f6fdb16c542ce3236f7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hectorqin <14220132+hectorqin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 03:22:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] feat(sidebar): nest child sessions under the session that
 started them

Render a session's childSessions under its row with their own provider
icon, a running indicator from the active-session state, and a muted
look once idle; clicking opens /session/<id> and selects the child's own
project. A project whose sessions are all children elsewhere is not
listed, and a running child keeps its parent in the running view.

Precedence: a session attached to a child-parent is shown only under
that parent; fork nesting still applies within each sibling group, so a
fork of a child nests under its source among the parent's children.
Live session_upserted events for children update them under their parent
instead of creating a project row; archive and rename reach nested rows.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
